am Kampong","ingredient/ayam-kampong"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/7/73/Zanthoxylum_acanthopodium_var._timbor_-_Kunming_Botanical_Garden_-_DSC03185.JPG/500px-Zanthoxylum_acanthopodium_var._timbor_-_Kunming_Botanical_Garden_-_DSC03185.JPG","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Daderot","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zanthoxylum_acanthopodium_var._timbor_-_Kunming_Botanical_Garden_-_DSC03185.JPG"}},"dish/hot-dry-noodles":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/hot-dry-noodles","n":"Hot dry noodles","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Hot dry noodles, sometimes called reganmian after the Chinese name, are a traditional dish of Wuhan, the capital of Hubei province in central China. Hot dry noodles have an 80-year history in Chinese food culture; they are unique because the noodles are not in a broth like most other Asian-style hot noodle dishes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hot-dry-noodles"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_dry_noodles"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine"],["Hubei cuisine","cuisine/hubei-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Alkaline noodles","ingredient/alkaline-noodles"],["Chili oil","ingredient/chili-oil"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Pickled carrots","ingredient/pickled-carrots"],["Sesame paste","ingredient/sesame-paste"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Woks of Life","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thewoksoflife.com","note":"Chinese and Chinese American recipes from the Leung family, running since 2013.","url":"https://thewoksoflife.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Chinese Cooking Demystified","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"youtube.com","note":"Technique-heavy YouTube channel on regional Chinese home and restaurant cookin