uli, Mudshuretuli and Keduretuli."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mujuretuli"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mujuretuli"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Georgian cuisine","cuisine/georgian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Georgian Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"georgianrecipes.net","note":"Recipe site dedicated to traditional Georgian dishes.","url":"https://georgianrecipes.net/about-georgian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Georgian cuisine","links":[["Achma","dish/achma"],["Ajika","dish/ajika"],["Akhasheni","dish/akhasheni"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chakapuli","dish/chakapuli"],["Chakhokhbili","dish/chakhokhbili"],["Chashushuli","dish/chashushuli"],["Chicken tabaka","dish/chicken-tabaka"],["Churchkhela","dish/churchkhela"],["Dambalkhacho","dish/dambalkhacho"],["Eggplant jam","dish/eggplant-jam"],["Gozinaki","dish/gozinaki"],["Khachapuri","dish/khachapuri"],["Kharcho","dish/kharcho"],["Khash (dish)","dish/khash-dish"],["Khvanchkara","dish/khvanchkara"],["Kindzmarauli","dish/kindzmarauli"],["Kubdari","dish/kubdari"],["Kuchmachi","dish/kuchmachi"],["Kvass","dish/kvass"],["Lobiani","dish/lobiani"],["Mchadi","dish/mchadi"],["Nadugi","dish/nadugi"],["Nigvziani badrijani","dish/nigvziani-badrijani"],["Pkhali","dish/pkhali"],["Shkmeruli","dish/shkmeruli"],["Tsolikouri","dish/tsolikouri"],["Tvishi (wine)","dish/tvishi-wine"]]}]},"dish/nasi-kapau":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/nasi-kapau","n":"Nasi kapau","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Nasi kapau is Minangkabau steamed rice topped with various choices of dishes, originated from Nagari Kapau, Bukittinggi, a tourism and culinary hotspot town in West Sumatra, Indonesia. It is often described as a Minang version of nasi ramas or nasi campur (mixed rice)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-nasi-kapau"},{"k